<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Bead nexus-p2m1x.21 (RDR-229 P3.3c, linda's rulings 2026-11-22): idx_chunk_orphaned_at_tenant_chash, an index on nexus.chunk_orphaned_at (tenant_id, chash).

    WHY. The chunks swap adds chunk_orphaned_at_chunk_id_fk, a foreign key from chunk_orphaned_at (tenant_id, collection_id, chash, embedding_model) to the
    chunks id key with ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE. Every delete or update of a chunk row then looks up the child rows by that key, and the only index
    chunk_orphaned_at has is its name primary key (tenant_id, collection, chash), which cannot seek past collection_id: a chunk delete would read every
    orphan-clock row of the tenant. The other two children already carry an index the lookup can use (catalog_document_chunks: idx_catalog_chunks_chash
    (tenant_id, chash), catalog-001; topic_assignments: idx_ta_tenant_doc_id_fk (tenant_id, doc_id), fk-001); Rdr229SwapMovesAfterTheSwapIntegrationTest
    shows the lookup of all three on its index. The chunks swap's verification waits for this index (Rdr229SwapMove), so the swap does not complete before a boot
    has built it.

    A BOOT MUST NEVER HANG OR HALT, AND A KILLED BUILD HEALS ON THE NEXT BOOT. One changeset, vectors-074-1, shaped like collections-001-2 (the repo's self-retrying
    changeset), with runInTransaction="false" because CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY cannot run inside a transaction:
      - preConditions onFail="CONTINUE" onError="CONTINUE", one sqlCheck: no VALID index of this name exists. While it holds, the changeset runs; when a VALID
        index exists (a manual pre-build) it is skipped, unrecorded, and retried at every boot, a visible member of the walk's retrying set
        (skipped_retrying_changesets) for as long as that index stands. Never HALT (a boot-time halt crash-loops an install, the no-wedge directive) and never
        MARK_RAN (that would record the changeset as run and stop it healing).
      - failOnError="false": a body that fails (the lock wait below ends, the build is cancelled or killed) is logged, the walk goes on, no DATABASECHANGELOG row
        is written (MarkChangeSetRanGenerator refuses a FAILED changeset), and the next boot retries it, exactly as a precondition skip.
      - THE HEAL. The check guarantees that whatever index of this name exists is INVALID (a build that died leaves one; IF NOT EXISTS would skip it and the
        changeset would be recorded with an index no query can use), so the body drops it first, DROP INDEX CONCURRENTLY IF EXISTS, and then builds. The drop is
        therefore never of a valid index: pg_index.indisvalid is read by the precondition, which is the only way to condition a CONCURRENTLY statement (it cannot run in
        a DO block). The two statements run one after the other, each on its own in autocommit, in the one changeset: a failure of either leaves nothing recorded.
      - THE BOUND. CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY and DROP INDEX CONCURRENTLY wait on older transactions as a lock wait, so SET lock_timeout = '30s' ends the wait. The
        setting is the migration session's and is reset after the build; a failing body leaves it on for the rest of that walk (the grants blocks that follow take
        no lock they could wait on for 30 s). A wait that ends is a skipped boot, not a failed one.
    The changeset is a CONTINUE changeset, so SchemaMigrator does not count it as schema work (it would otherwise end every running per-collection index build at the
    first boot that carries it): its body takes SHARE UPDATE EXCLUSIVE on nexus.chunk_orphaned_at and nothing on nexus.chunks or a chunk leaf, and a CREATE INDEX
    CONCURRENTLY on a leaf holds no lock on chunk_orphaned_at. tests/test_changelog_continue_precondition_chunks_lint.py bars a CONTINUE body from naming a table that
    holds a foreign key into chunks, because a DROP or ALTER of one takes ACCESS EXCLUSIVE on every chunk leaf; it now lets the one statement shape that takes no such lock
    through (CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY on that table) and the changeset is on its allowlist with this argument.

    DATA EFFECT: none. The index is built over existing rows and changes no row; its maintenance cost on writes is one more btree entry per orphan-clock row.
    nexus.chunk_orphaned_at holds one row per chunk that lost its last owner, so the build is short. The number follows vectors-073 and is provisional until the
    final rebase. After vectors-073, before the grants-nexus-svc.xml runAlways block.
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <changeSet id="vectors-074-1" author="nexus-p2m1x.21" runInTransaction="false" failOnError="false">
        <preConditions onFail="CONTINUE" onError="CONTINUE">
            <sqlCheck expectedResult="0">SELECT COUNT(*) FROM pg_index i JOIN pg_class c ON c.oid = i.indexrelid JOIN pg_namespace n ON n.oid = c.relnamespace WHERE n.nspname = 'nexus' AND c.relname = 'idx_chunk_orphaned_at_tenant_chash' AND i.indisvalid</sqlCheck>
        </preConditions>
        <comment>nexus.chunk_orphaned_at (tenant_id, chash): the child-side lookup of the chunk's id key, chunk_orphaned_at_chunk_id_fk (RDR-229 P3.3c). Self-retrying (onFail CONTINUE, failOnError false): drops an INVALID leftover of the index, then builds it, each CONCURRENTLY, outside a transaction, under lock_timeout 30 s. DATA EFFECT: none. The rollback drops the index.</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
SET lock_timeout = '30s';
DROP INDEX CONCURRENTLY IF EXISTS nexus.idx_chunk_orphaned_at_tenant_chash;
CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY IF NOT EXISTS idx_chunk_orphaned_at_tenant_chash
    ON nexus.chunk_orphaned_at (tenant_id, chash);
RESET lock_timeout;
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
DROP INDEX CONCURRENTLY IF EXISTS nexus.idx_chunk_orphaned_at_tenant_chash;
            </sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
